  58: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
  59:     """
  60:     Recolor the monochrome foreground mask by its unique tiling into 2x2 squares and three 2x2 L-tromino orientations.
  61: 
  62:     Input structure
  63:     - The background is the dominant color.
  64:     - All non-background pixels have one foreground color and form a mask that can be tiled by small 2x2-based sprites.
  65: 
  66:     Rule
  67:     - Cover the foreground exactly once with translated tiles: a filled 2x2 square, an L missing the upper-left cell, an L missing the lower-left cell, or an L missing the upper-right cell.
  68:     - Recolor those four tile shapes blue, red, green, and yellow respectively.
  69:     - Keep background pixels unchanged.
  70: 
  71:     Key insight
  72:     - Some L-trominoes interlock, so their missing corner may be occupied by another tile; the invariant is the unique exact cover of foreground cells, not local 2x2 background.
  73:     """
